+- **Bounded staleness** does not wait for writes to propagate, but places an
+  explicit ceiling on how stale a read may be. It reads the freshest timestamp
+  that is no more than the configured duration behind the system's current
+  timestamp, so reads avoid the wait imposed by Strict Serializable while
+  bounding staleness (unlike Serializable). If no timestamp within the bound is
+  available, the query returns an error instead of blocking. See [Bounded
+  staleness](#bounded-staleness).
+
+## Bounded staleness
+
+Bounded staleness lets you read data that is no older than a duration you
+choose, without waiting for recent writes to propagate through materialized
+views and indexes. It is modeled on bounded-staleness reads in systems such as
+Spanner.
+
+### Syntax
+
+```mzsql
+SET TRANSACTION_ISOLATION TO 'BOUNDED STALENESS <duration>';
+```
+
+`<duration>` is a human-readable duration such as `5s`, `500ms`, or `1m30s`. A
+zero duration is rejected. There is no upper cap on the duration; large bounds
+behave similarly to Serializable when input frontiers stay within the bound.
+
+### Semantics
+
+Under bounded staleness, Materialize selects the freshest timestamp that is at
+most `<duration>` behind the system's current timestamp, without waiting on
+input frontiers. This gives you an explicit guarantee of the form "data no
+older than `<duration>`" rather than a guarantee of perfect freshness.
+
+If no timestamp within the bound is available (for example, because an input
+lags by more than `<duration>`), the query fails with SQLSTATE `40001`
+(serialization failure) instead of blocking. This error is raised before the
+query is dispatched to a cluster, so the failure mode does not depend on your
+cluster configuration.
+
+### Restrictions
+
+- Bounded staleness is read-only. `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`, and `COPY FROM`
+  are rejected under this isolation level.
+- Bounded staleness cannot be combined with
+  [`real_time_recency`](#real-time-recency). Setting `real_time_recency = on`
+  while using bounded staleness is rejected.
+- Bounded staleness is only supported on the wall-clock (`EpochMilliseconds`)
+  timeline. Queries that touch other timelines are rejected.
+
+### Feature flag
+
+Bounded staleness is gated behind the `enable_bounded_staleness_isolation`
+feature flag. Until the flag is enabled, setting
+`TRANSACTION_ISOLATION` to a bounded-staleness value fails at planning time.
+
